Z||000000||slick||07-04-99||02:45 PM||||help! my 88 2.5l coupe starts and runs fine when cool and on inital start up. but after being driven on warm days,on restart it will turn over, idle up and down, then stall. this will occur several times, then run fine.<br>it is DEFINITELY heat related. if i leave the deck lid up this problem doesn't occur.<br>I have replaced : the ecm, crank position sensor, ignition module, coils, wires, plugs, battery, o2 sensor,pcv, air filter, thermostat and coolant. the starter and fuel pump seem ok.the vehicle doesn't overheat. could it be thetps, map sensor,or iac valve ?<br>any help will be appreciated.
