Z||000004||theogre||07-06-99||07:42 PM||||I haven't had time to reread that thread..... did that one mention disconnecting the slagging tach filter. If it didn't, try that.<p>one thing that could be happening.... it's rare but posible...... take the center console off. the shifter bezel is held by 4 screw under the ashtrays. the back part is held by 2 screws under the bezel, and 2 under the storage box. It's posible the ECM is hot. This would let it stay cooler for testing. if the situation improves, you may have to replace the ECM. It may have a bad internal connection or something that is flipping out when hot.
